Nikon Camera Calibration Data
-----------------------------

OpenRAW Native includes numeric Nikon D500, 1 J5, Z5, and Z f camera-calibration constants
published as Adobe DNG Converter profile data. The OpenRAW transform and render
implementation is project-authored. LibRaw was used as a development reference
and validation oracle; no LibRaw code or binary is bundled as a runtime
dependency.

Reference table:
https://github.com/LibRaw/LibRaw/blob/master/src/tables/colordata.cpp

Z5 uses the DNG Converter 13.2 calibration values recorded in RawTherapee's
camera-data table, not its processing code or a RawTherapee runtime:
https://github.com/RawTherapee/RawTherapee/blob/dev/rtengine/camconst.json

Nikon Compression Format Data
----------------------------

The native Huffman tables are numeric file-format constants. D20 decoding uses
OpenRAW's own bitstream reader and validates/interpolates the curve stored in
the input NEF. Independent development comparisons do not introduce a LibRaw
runtime dependency. Format-data reference:
https://github.com/LibRaw/LibRaw/blob/master/src/decoders/decoders_dcraw.cpp

Newer Nikon compression mode identifiers and the MakerNote 0x0051 field offset
follow the ExifTool Nikon tag reference. OpenRAW's metadata parser is
project-authored. Mode identification alone does not establish decoding support.
https://github.com/exiftool/exiftool/blob/master/lib/Image/ExifTool/Nikon.pm

The read-only HE research diagnostic uses published stream-framing facts and
local file observations, not external decoder implementation code.
https://github.com/zidage/LibRaw/blob/main_alcedo/doc/nikon_he_public_algorithm.md

The guarded Z f HE/HE* entropy, inverse-wavelet, and color-lifting modules are project-authored from
format facts, mathematical operations, and synthetic/local numerical validation.
Technical references include the JPEG XS decoder documentation and the uniform
quantizer reconstruction described by the SVT-JPEG-XS project. No SVT-JPEG-XS or
LibRaw decoder implementation, lookup-table implementation, or binary is bundled.
The independently compiled reference stays outside the distributed app and is
used only to compare numeric results during development.
https://github.com/OpenVisualCloud/SVT-JPEG-XS/blob/main/documentation/decoder/svt-jpegxs-decoder-design.md
https://github.com/OpenVisualCloud/SVT-JPEG-XS/blob/main/Source/Lib/Decoder/Codec/Dequant.c

The inverse color lift also uses the mathematical framework described by
Richter et al., Bayer CFA Pattern Compression With JPEG XS (2021).
https://doi.org/10.1109/TIP.2021.3095421
OpenRAW computes its own two-sided quadratic nonlinear mapping for the verified
Z f profile. This is an approximation, not a copied reference decoder LUT or a
claim of exact Nikon curve reproduction.

This attribution and the MIT source license do not establish patent clearance
for the HE/JPEG XS implementation; distribution requires a separate review.

